## Usage

<!-- stacks:fill The `cargo add` line people should run, in a bash code block. -->

```rust
use crate_name::{Error, Rules, Slug};

fn main() -> Result<(), Error> {
    let slug: Slug = "hello-world".parse()?;
    assert_eq!(slug.as_str(), "hello-world");

    let short = Rules::with_max_len(5)?;
    assert!(short.parse("hello-world").is_err());
    Ok(())
}
```

Every `rust` block in this file runs as a doctest, so keep the examples compiling.

## Features

- `serde`: `Serialize` and `Deserialize` for `Slug`, as a string that is validated when read.

